course: dictionary
lesson: 885
title: Light from living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bioluminescence is a long word, but you can work out its meaning from the words around it. «Some fungi glow in the dark with a soft green light, called bioluminescence, made by a chemical reaction inside them.» The words called and made by tell you that the long word names this glow. Swap in «the glow made by living things» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Many deep-sea animals make their own light, called bioluminescence, to find food, lure prey and signal.» The purpose clues help here: the light is used to find food and to signal. Lure means to tempt with a bait, and prey means animals that are hunted for food, so the anglerfish's glowing lure is a kind of bait.
explain: The same idea works for other forms of the word. Bioluminescent is the adjective, so «bioluminescent sparkles» means sparkles made by living things. When you meet a new science word, look for the clues first, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Bioluminescence means light made by living things.
fact: Fireflies, glow-worms, some fungi and many deep-sea animals show bioluminescence.
fact: Animals use bioluminescence to attract mates, lure prey, scare predators or hide.
fact: The light is made by a chemical reaction inside the body, and it gives off little heat.
fact: The adjective is bioluminescent, as in «bioluminescent sparkles in the sea».
exercise: «Some fungi glow in the dark with a soft green light, called bioluminescence.» What does bioluminescence mean? | *Light made by living things | A kind of dark, cold rock | Sparkling water from a tap | Heat made by machines
exercise: Why do many deep-sea animals use bioluminescence? | To hide the sea floor from divers | To keep warm in cold water | *To find food, lure prey and signal | To make the sea taste salty
exercise: Find and copy the word that means shining with light in «Some fungi glow in the dark with a soft green light». | chemical | *glow | fungi | green
test: Blue sparkles in the sea at night are caused by tiny plankton. What is this glow called? | Camouflage | *Bioluminescence | Photosynthesis | Hibernation
test: Which of these is an example of bioluminescence? | A torch switched on in a cave | Sunlight on a lamp | Light from a candle | *A glow-worm glowing in the grass
exam: The sentence says bioluminescence is «made by a chemical reaction inside them». What does this tell you? | It comes from the sun | *It comes from a chemical reaction inside the living thing | It is made by a torch | It is a kind of rock
